| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/compaction/working_set.dart | 💡 suggestion flatten whitespace in rendered file paths — the goal line does paths don t goalline collapses whitespace so the block is one line per fact dart final flat recitation goal replaceall regexp r s trim but file paths render verbatim dart if kept isnotempty filesheading kept map p p a path argument containing n legal in posix filenames and model emitted into tool arguments renders multi line inside the system notice block after a compaction these tool calls are hidden — the working set block is the only place that string survives past the fold so a newline carrying path can inject arbitrary extra lines into a system tagged block and spoof its structure fake file entries fake counting tail lines the budgets still hold the char budget loop drops offending files so this is structure spoofing not a budget bypass mirror the goal line s treatment e g flatten each path before rendering p replaceall regexp r s or skip paths that contain whitespace control chars — one line consistent hardening of the new surface |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

